## Day 71 Session Plan — Three tasks, one theme: **make the money count**

### Task 1: Enable prompt caching via yoagent's CacheConfig
Self-driven (capability gap). yoagent 0.8 has CacheConfig with `with_cache_config()` — yoyo never calls it. One line in agent_builder.rs enables automatic prompt caching for Anthropic, which can save 60-90% on input token costs for multi-turn conversations. This is the "don't reinvent the wheel" principle — the feature is right there, just unwired. Files: src/agent_builder.rs.

### Task 2: Add native desktop notifications on long completions
**Self-driven (competitive gap).** Currently yoyo rings the terminal bell after 3s. Desktop notifications (macOS osascript, Linux notify-send, Windows PowerShell toast) fire after 10s for genuinely long waits. No external crates — pure shell commands via std::process::Command. Aider has this; yoyo doesn't. Files: src/format/mod.rs, src/main.rs, src/help.rs.

### Task 3: Show cache hit rate in /cost and /tokens displays
Self-driven (UX). Completes the caching story from Task 1 — adds format_cache_stats() using yoagent's `Usage::cache_hit_rate() and wires it into /cost and /tokens` output so users can see caching is working and how much it's saving. Files: src/format/cost.rs, `src/commands_info.rs`.

